        "description": "<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">You&rsquo;re interning at \"LitHaven Library\", tasked with organizing their digital catalog. The head librarian wants to highlight the&nbsp;<strong>newest additions</strong>&nbsp;but notices ISBN codes in the database embed publication years. They ask:&nbsp;\"Can you extract the publication year from the ISBN and list the latest books?\"</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The&nbsp;<strong>'books'</strong>&nbsp;table contains columns&nbsp;<strong>'isbn'</strong>&nbsp;(primary key, format like 'YYYYTitle...'),&nbsp;<strong>'title'</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>'author'</strong>, and&nbsp;<strong>'genre'</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">Your task is to extract the first 4 characters of the ISBN as the&nbsp;<strong>'publication_year'</strong>, then list the&nbsp;<strong>top 5 most recent books</strong>&nbsp;sorted by publication year (newest first). If years tie, sort by title alphabetically.</p>\n<p class=\"ds-markdown-paragraph\">The output columns should Include <strong>'title'</strong>,&nbsp;<strong>'author'</strong>, and&nbsp;<strong>'publication_year'</strong>, ordered by&nbsp;<strong>'publication_year'</strong>&nbsp;descending, then&nbsp;<strong>'title'</strong> ascending.</p>",
