        "description": "<p>In the Cosmic Archives, librarians want to spotlight scrolls whose titles evoke the heavens and are currently borrowed by scholars, helping them track popular celestial lore.</p>\n<p>You are given two tables: &lsquo;scrolls&rsquo; and &lsquo;loans&rsquo;.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The &lsquo;scrolls&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;scroll_id&rsquo; and &lsquo;title&rsquo;. Each row names one manuscript.</li>\n<li>The &lsquo;loans&rsquo; table contains &lsquo;loan_id&rsquo;, &lsquo;scroll_id&rsquo;, and &lsquo;returned_date&rsquo;. Each row logs when a scroll was borrowed and when it was returned (NULL if still on loan).</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"379\" data-end=\"399\">You are required to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"403\" data-end=\"482\">Identify scrolls whose title contains the word <strong data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"462\">\"star\"</strong> (case-insensitive).</li>\n<li data-start=\"485\" data-end=\"577\">Count how many of those scrolls are <strong data-start=\"521\" data-end=\"542\">currently on loan</strong> (i.e., 'returned_date' is NULL).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The output columns should be &lsquo;title&rsquo; and &lsquo;active_loans&rsquo;, ordered by &lsquo;active_loans&rsquo; descending, then by &lsquo;title&rsquo; ascending order.</p>",
