        "difficulty": "easy",
        "description": "<p data-start=\"23\" data-end=\"133\">As the data specialist for Cream &amp; Tours, you were tasked with optimizing their new ice-cream rewards program. The marketing team needed to match free sundae flavors to each traveler's destination vibe, but with thousands of bookings across beach resorts, mountain retreats, and city escapes, manual categorization was impossible.</p>\n<p data-start=\"23\" data-end=\"133\">You are given two tables, 'customers' and 'bookings', that store travel-related data for a tourism agency.</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"137\" data-end=\"261\">The 'customers' table contains 'customer_id' and 'name', representing the unique identifier and name of each customer.</li>\n<li data-start=\"264\" data-end=\"407\">The 'bookings' table contains 'booking_id', 'customer_id', and 'destination', capturing each customer's travel booking and destination.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"409\" data-end=\"510\">Write a query to categorize each booking based on the 'destination' and label it as a type of trip.</p>\n<ul>\n<li data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"609\">If the 'destination' contains the substring 'Beach' or 'Island', classify it as 'Tropical'.</li>\n<li data-start=\"612\" data-end=\"692\">If the 'destination' contains 'Mountain' or 'Hike', classify it as 'Alpine'.</li>\n<li data-start=\"695\" data-end=\"734\">Otherwise, classify it as 'Standard'.</li>\n</ul>\n<p data-start=\"736\" data-end=\"827\">Return the customer's name, their destination, and the computed trip type for each booking.</p>\n<p data-start=\"829\" data-end=\"996\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">The final output should include the columns 'name', 'destination', and 'trip_type', sorted by 'name' in ascending order and 'destination' in ascending order.</p>",
